                <pb facs="0621" n="515" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg515"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the American Legation.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-01-30"><hi rendition="#italic">January 30,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Root, referring to assurance by Cuban treasury under date of July 27, 1904,
                    to Mr. Hawley, in reply to inquiry respecting benefit of reciprocity treaty rate
                    to foreign rice milled in this country and shipped to Cuba by Seaboard Rice
                    Milling Company, instructs the legation to urge upon Cuban Government granting
                    of benefit to their shipment of 350 bags per <hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Titlis</hi>, and to intended shipment of about 2,000 bags, bought for such
                    shipment by them and entailing great loss if not shipped under that benefit. The
                    company’s agents at Habana, Louis G. Smith &amp; Co., may be consulted for
                    needed detail.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
